# Suggestion Roadmap

Current status: the agreed Movies, Books, and Music improvements are implemented, tested, and ready to commit.

## Done

- [x] Use only the active section's Favorites (`topTen`) as positive taste evidence.
- [x] Treat For Later, recent, liked/completed, and rejected items only as exclusions.
- [x] Keep taste badges out of suggestion selection and ranking.
- [x] Add `FAST_MODEL_NAME` / `OPENAI_FAST_MODEL`, with safe fallback to the main model.
- [x] Retry an unusable fast-model result once with the main model and record the model role for QA.
- [x] Generate up to five ranked Movie/Series candidates, verify them in parallel with Wikidata, and select the first safe result.
- [x] Reject Movie/Series title-creator conflicts and check verified cross-language aliases for duplicates.
- [x] Use official original identity across Movies, Books, and Music: Persian originals stay Persian; foreign works keep their official English/international identity.
- [x] Prevent interface language, Favorite script, mood, and request wording from translating titles or creators.
- [x] Remove Google Books and retrieval-first ranking from the active Book suggestion flow.
- [x] Generate five ranked Book identities and verify up to five in order within the existing deadline.
- [x] Verify Books with exact Open Library title-author matching, then strict Wikidata fallback.
- [x] Accept exact safe Open Library edition-title aliases while rejecting combined records, study guides, notes, summaries, analysis, criticism, companions, and workbooks.
- [x] Allow unusual Wikidata Book classifications only when the exact title and P50 author relationship match; reject Movie/TV entities.
- [x] Cache verified Book identities and explicit mismatches, but never cache complete catalogue outages.
- [x] Update the suggestion QA lab and documentation for the new flow.
- [x] Complete initial manual QA for Movies, Books, and Music.
- [x] Pass lint, architecture checks, translation validation, unit tests, integration tests, and production dependency audit.

## Cleanup completed

- [x] Remove retired Book retrieval/ranking modules, their old Google Books implementation, and dedicated obsolete tests.
- [x] Remove retired Persian Book, Movie, and Music display resolvers and their dedicated obsolete tests after confirming no production imports remain.

## Later (only if testing shows a need)

- [ ] Add persistent/shared catalogue-verification caching if repeated verification traffic becomes a measurable performance or rate-limit problem. The current cache is bounded and in memory.
- [ ] Improve Persian display for international Music only if users struggle to recognize or search the official catalogue names.
- [ ] Add a trusted ratings provider only if ratings become a product requirement; ratings must never gate suggestions.

## Needs discussion before implementation

- [ ] Decide whether Movies need an extra fast-model reranking call. Current manual results are good; adding it would increase latency and cost.
- [ ] Decide whether Books should request a second replacement batch when all five candidates fail verification. This could reduce failures but would increase latency, provider usage, and catalogue calls.
